course: dictionary
lesson: 1931
title: One word, many meanings: command
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Command can be a verb or a noun, and it can mean different things. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. The clues tell you what kind of command is meant. «Type a command to save the file.» Here the words type and file tell you a command is an instruction for a computer.
explain: «The captain gave a command, and the crew raised the sails.» A command is an order, and the crew obey it. You can test this by swapping in the meaning: "The captain gave an order, and the crew raised the sails." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Command can also mean skill with something. «Maya has a good command of French.» Maya is not ordering French about. A good command of French means she knows it well. The word of tells you that a command is held of something.
explain: Some commands are sentences. «Shut the door!» is a command sentence. It tells someone to do something, and the word you is not written, but it is understood. «Help!», «Run!» and «Listen!» are one-word commands, and they are complete sentences too.
fact: Command can be a verb (to command) or a noun (a command).
fact: «Command» means to tell someone officially to do something, or an order.
fact: «Command» can mean control of a group, such as an army: «The general is in command.»
fact: «Command» can mean knowledge and skill: «a good command of English».
fact: «Command» can mean an instruction to a computer: «type a command».
exercise: «Type the command to save the file.» What does command mean here? | *An instruction a computer follows | A type of cake | A fancy hat | To laugh loudly
exercise: «The captain gave a command, and the crew raised the sails.» What is a command here? | A question about the weather | A friendly wave | *An order | A kind of boat
exercise: «Shut the door!» is a command sentence. Find and copy the word that tells you what to do. | door | the | *Shut
test: «Maya has a good command of French.» What does command mean here? | To order someone about | *Knowledge and skill at something | To look over a valley | A kind of robot
test: «The castle commands the valley.» What does commands mean here? | Walks down into the valley | Orders the valley to stop | *Has a view over the valley | Pays for the valley
exam: Which sentence is a command? | Did you see the bird? | The sun is hot. | *Listen! | My bike is red.
